    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d71">

                <pb facs="0072" n="52" sameAs="frus:frus1864p3/pg52"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr. Dayton</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 506.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1864-03-17"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >March</hi> 17, 1864.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I herewith transmit to you, for your
                    information, the copy of a translation of a note of the 11th instant from Mr. L.
                    de Geofroy, the chargé d’affaires of France, and of the reply from this
                    department of the 12th instant, relative to the presence of United States troops
                    in Matamoras.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">William L. Dayton</hi> Esq., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                    <p>[For enclosures see correspondence with the French legation.]</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
